  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Mollicellin N may be involved in the biological activity targeting SNU-449 through multiple indirect pathways. The final scores indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship between Mollicellin N and SNU-449, as it is indirectly linked through the compound 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which acts as a target of both Mollicellin N and NB13. This pathway connects Mollicellin N to SNU-449, suggesting a potential role in modulating cellular processes in the cancer cell line SNU-449. Additionally, Mollicellin N is also linked to P2X purinoceptor 7, which is targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and this compound further leads to SNU-449. The integration of these pathways highlights a complex network of interactions, where Mollicellin N may influence SNU-449 through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving receptor activation or enzyme inhibition. The evidence supports a possible role for Mollicellin N in modulating the activity of SNU-449, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated."
